# Paths excluded from Semgrep SAST (gitignore syntax).

# Static redirect stub pages served by GitHub Pages (see redirect-github-io.yml).
# Semgrep's missing-integrity rule flags the <link rel="canonical"> tag, but
# Subresource Integrity does not apply to a canonical link (no subresource is
# fetched, and there is no stable hash for a live page). An inline `nosemgrep`
# does not help here: Semgrep still emits the finding into SARIF as a suppressed
# result, which GitHub code scanning surfaces as an open alert. Excluding these
# trivial redirect stubs keeps the SARIF clean.
.github/redirect/
